pipeline: simple: do not give the viewfinder a default size that the software ISP cannot sustain

generateConfiguration() picks the largest size the pipeline can produce, for
every role, and its own comment says so:

    /*
     * Create the stream configurations. Take the first entry in the formats
     * map as the default, for lack of a better option.
     *
     * \todo Implement a better way to pick the default format
     */

When processing goes through the CPU, that maximum is the full sensor
resolution and is far beyond real time. An application that does not ask for a
size of its own -and plasma-camera does not: it comes in through Qt6 Multimedia
and requests the Viewfinder role- is left with an unusable viewfinder.

MEASURED on an SM7150 (Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC) with a 64 Mpx IMX682, frames per
second delivered against output size:

    2312x1304   (3.0 Mpx)   52.5 fps
    3840x2160   (8.3 Mpx)   27.5 fps, dropping to 13.8
    4624x3472  (16.1 Mpx)    7.2 fps
    9248x6944  (64.2 Mpx)   unusable

So for the roles that are LIVE -Viewfinder and VideoRecording- the largest
sensor configuration that fits within a pixel budget is chosen. StillCapture and
Raw keep the full resolution, which is exactly what they are for.

It only applies when the software ISP is in use. With a hardware converter the
maximum is still reasonable and there is no reason to touch it.
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1489,6 +1489,48 @@
 		cfg.pixelFormat = formats.begin()->first;
 		cfg.size = formats.begin()->second[0].max;
 
+		/*
+		 * Don't default a viewfinder to a size the software ISP cannot
+		 * sustain.
+		 *
+		 * The size above is the largest the pipeline can produce, which
+		 * for a raw sensor is its full resolution. When the debayering
+		 * runs on the CPU that is often far beyond real time, and an
+		 * application that does not request a size of its own ends up
+		 * with an unusable preview.
+		 *
+		 * Measured on an SM7150 phone (Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC) with a 64 MP
+		 * IMX682, delivered frames per second against output size:
+		 *
+		 *     2312x1304   (3.0 MP)   52.5 fps
+		 *     3840x2160   (8.3 MP)   27.5 fps, dropping to 13.8
+		 *     4624x3472  (16.1 MP)    7.2 fps
+		 *     9248x6944  (64.2 MP)   unusable
+		 *
+		 * So pick, for the roles that are meant to be live, the largest
+		 * sensor configuration that stays within a budget. Still capture
+		 * and raw keep the full resolution, which is what they are for.
+		 */
+		if (data->swIsp_ &&
+		    (role == StreamRole::Viewfinder ||
+		     role == StreamRole::VideoRecording)) {
+			constexpr unsigned int kSwIspLivePixelBudget = 4000000;
+			Size live;
+
+			for (const SimpleCameraData::Configuration &c : data->configs_) {
+				unsigned int area = c.captureSize.width *
+						    c.captureSize.height;
+
+				if (area > kSwIspLivePixelBudget)
+					continue;
+				if (area > live.width * live.height)
+					live = c.captureSize;
+			}
+
+			if (!live.isNull() && live < cfg.size)
+				cfg.size = live;
+		}
+
 		config->addConfiguration(cfg);
 	}
 
